  "goodToKnow": "Die Geldstrafe is a fine imposed for a crime: eine Geldstrafe von 90 Tagessätzen. German courts use a day-fine system: the number of Tagessätze reflects the crime, and the amount of each reflects the offender's daily income, so fines are fairer for rich and poor. Fines of more than 90 Tagessätze show up on a Führungszeugnis (certificate of good conduct). Minor traffic fines are a Bußgeld or Verwarnungsgeld, and a parking ticket is casually ein Knöllchen. Plural: die Geldstrafen."
